WEBVTT

00:00.880 --> 00:02.590
I'm back!

00:02.590 --> 00:03.850
And... Huh?

00:04.500 --> 00:06.110
No one's here.

00:08.270 --> 00:09.280
Where did they all—

00:09.280 --> 00:12.540
It's my first time. 
I don't know much about this.

00:13.510 --> 00:15.000
Don't worry.

00:15.000 --> 00:17.370
<i>Hayato-kun... Kiku-chan?</i>

00:17.370 --> 00:19.790
I'll teach you what to do.

00:19.790 --> 00:21.750
Okay. Thanks.

00:21.750 --> 00:25.290
First, you put this in between these...

00:25.760 --> 00:26.830
Huh?

00:27.450 --> 00:30.570
Yours is a little too big, Hayato-kun...

00:30.570 --> 00:33.130
Is it? Isn't this normal?

00:33.130 --> 00:34.720
It's definitely on the big side.

00:35.880 --> 00:38.720
It's not going to go in very well like that.

00:39.460 --> 00:42.350
Excuse me! Just what are you 
putting in where?!

00:43.200 --> 00:45.640
...is what I was thinking, but...

00:46.210 --> 00:48.640
I get it! You were talking about 
a toasted sandwich!

00:48.640 --> 00:53.160
You were saying Hayato-kun cut the tomato 
too big to fit inside it, right?!

00:53.160 --> 00:54.790
O-Of course I knew that!

00:55.520 --> 00:57.030
Welcome back.

01:13.090 --> 01:15.670
<b></b>The Café Terrace and Its Goddesses

02:28.360 --> 02:33.240
Okay, Hayato-kun. Kiku-chan and I 
will be teaching you how to cook.

02:30.420 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.450 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.490 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.520 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.560 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.590 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.630 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.670 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.700 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.740 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.770 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.810 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.840 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.880 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.920 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.950 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:30.990 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:31.020 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:31.060 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:31.090 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:31.130 --> 02:36.130
<b>Episode 6: "Two Months!"</b>

02:33.240 --> 02:35.260
You'd better be grateful.

02:35.260 --> 02:38.160
Actually, just Shiragiku is fine.

02:38.160 --> 02:40.800
We're only making toasted 
sandwiches to start with.

02:41.430 --> 02:42.880
Big talk coming from you!

02:42.880 --> 02:45.690
Just look at this failure! 
What a waste of food!

02:45.690 --> 02:48.960
Oh, shut up! 
I'm going to eat it myself, okay?

02:48.960 --> 02:51.900
He started making it on his own...

02:52.250 --> 02:55.730
Well, a toasted sandwich 
seems like it should be easy.

02:56.630 --> 03:00.780
I do think it's great that 
you're so motivated, though.

03:00.780 --> 03:03.240
R-Really?

03:03.240 --> 03:06.060
I mean, I <i>am</i> the owner, after all.

03:04.530 --> 03:07.950
<i>Why does he look so happy 
over a little compliment like that?</i>

03:08.360 --> 03:09.420
She's right.

03:09.420 --> 03:13.160
I do agree that that's the right attitude 
for a café owner to have.

03:13.160 --> 03:14.290
Huh?

03:15.810 --> 03:16.950
Really?

03:18.240 --> 03:19.300
Thanks.

03:26.150 --> 03:28.890
Hey! Don't just touch me 
like we're best friends!

03:28.890 --> 03:31.120
That hurt! What'd you do that for?!

03:31.120 --> 03:32.100
What's your problem?!

03:34.500 --> 03:35.810
What's wrong?

03:35.810 --> 03:38.230
Huh? Oh, uh...

03:39.270 --> 03:41.960
Um... Okay, let's get started!

03:41.960 --> 03:42.910
Sure.

03:45.490 --> 03:47.240
Hadoken!

03:51.830 --> 03:52.860
Did it come out?!

03:52.860 --> 03:53.790
Did what come out?

03:53.790 --> 03:55.630
The Hadoken!

03:55.630 --> 03:57.000
What's a Hadoken?

03:57.260 --> 03:58.040
Huh?

03:58.660 --> 04:00.970
Uh, I'm not actually sure.

04:02.690 --> 04:04.720
Hey, can I go now?

04:05.020 --> 04:08.080
Now lay the ham on top of the grated carrot.

04:08.080 --> 04:08.930
Okay.

04:08.930 --> 04:11.850
Oh, put the tomato more toward the center.

04:12.290 --> 04:13.140
Like this?

04:13.140 --> 04:16.060
Yeah, that's it! Just like that!

04:16.060 --> 04:19.030
Huh. This isn't as easy as I thought.

04:24.470 --> 04:26.160
Look, Okiku-chan!

04:26.160 --> 04:27.620
Okiku-chan?

04:27.620 --> 04:30.870
Isn't a toasted ham sandwich kinda dated?

04:31.330 --> 04:35.330
I think a sandwich with uncured ham 
and pastrami is better.

04:35.840 --> 04:39.840
But this is how Grandma 
taught me to make them.

04:40.270 --> 04:43.300
We need to update the menu 
to keep up with the times.

04:43.300 --> 04:46.430
If Grandma were still here, 
that's what she'd do.

04:46.430 --> 04:50.010
But the old regulars say they prefer this.

04:50.480 --> 04:52.120
You need to think about the younger—

04:52.120 --> 04:55.020
I don't care what it is. 
Just teach me how to make it.

04:56.220 --> 04:58.160
Well, which one do <i>you</i> prefer?!

04:58.160 --> 04:59.530
You're the owner!

05:00.660 --> 05:04.530
I mean, I guess Grandma's menu 
is a little old-fashioned.

05:05.600 --> 05:07.530
How cruel! How...

05:07.950 --> 05:10.250
How can you say that in front 
of Grandma's portrait?!

05:10.250 --> 05:11.430
Easily.

05:11.430 --> 05:14.160
I've been saying it 
since she was alive, in fact.

05:14.520 --> 05:18.420
Have you ever even eaten 
Grandma's toasted sandwiches?

05:19.060 --> 05:20.360
Actually, maybe not...

05:20.360 --> 05:21.750
I'll make you one!

05:22.410 --> 05:27.930
I'll make you the Familia toasted sandwich, 
copied directly from Grandma's!

05:28.890 --> 05:34.640
In that case, I'll make you a trendy 
sandwich aimed at younger customers.

05:38.180 --> 05:41.150
What is even happening here? 
Just teach me how to make one.

05:42.080 --> 05:43.860
Mussy Mustache Girls.

05:43.860 --> 05:45.860
What? Don't you think that's kinda dorky?

05:45.860 --> 05:48.060
We don't even have mustaches.

05:48.060 --> 05:50.600
Then how about Mustache Girls Are Mussy?

05:50.600 --> 05:51.740
Same issue...

05:53.240 --> 05:54.740
Mustache Dance?

05:55.860 --> 05:57.870
Can we get away from mustaches for a minute?

05:57.870 --> 06:01.290
I don't think there's anything wrong 
with our current name.

05:58.330 --> 05:59.330
<b></b>Calling

05:58.330 --> 05:59.330
<b></b>Remind Me

05:58.330 --> 05:59.330
<b></b>Message

05:58.330 --> 05:59.330
<b></b>Accept

05:58.330 --> 05:59.330
<b></b>Decline

06:03.170 --> 06:04.890
Aren't you gonna answer that?

06:04.890 --> 06:06.670
Oh... Nah.

06:09.760 --> 06:13.340
This is the toasted sandwich 
Grandma taught me to make.

06:15.000 --> 06:18.690
Done! Here's my uncured ham 
and pastrami sandwich!

06:21.770 --> 06:22.800
Hayato-kun!

06:22.800 --> 06:23.860
Hey!

06:24.340 --> 06:27.570
How long is it gonna take you 
to eat your own failed attempts?!

06:28.000 --> 06:30.820
Well, there's still a bunch left.

06:30.820 --> 06:33.040
Try the ones we made,

06:33.040 --> 06:35.240
and pick the one you like better!

06:35.240 --> 06:37.500
Is it mine or Kiku-chan's?

06:46.110 --> 06:49.400
I can't. I'm so full, 
I can't eat another bite.

06:50.590 --> 06:54.850
You should've saved enough room to try ours!

06:55.100 --> 06:56.230
Sorry...

06:57.510 --> 06:59.020
Just a tiny bit?

06:59.020 --> 07:01.420
No, I seriously can't.

07:01.980 --> 07:03.740
H-Hey!

07:03.740 --> 07:06.650
But I pretty much know how to make them now.

07:06.650 --> 07:10.150
Have the other three decide 
which one tastes better.

07:10.150 --> 07:13.000
I'm gonna go lie down in my room.

07:15.510 --> 07:18.230
<i>I wanted Hayato-kun to tell me...</i>

07:20.070 --> 07:23.420
<i>...that he liked mine better.</i>

07:26.950 --> 07:32.300
I refuse to get forced into a choice 
that's gonna offend someone either way.

07:33.000 --> 07:34.680
Oh, wow!

07:36.950 --> 07:40.140
Your sandwich tastes great, Riho-chan!

07:40.760 --> 07:43.350
Yours is really good, too!

07:43.350 --> 07:46.320
Well, hey. Looks like you two get along fine.

07:46.320 --> 07:48.190
What? Of course we do.

07:48.190 --> 07:50.410
We weren't fighting or anything. Right?

07:51.240 --> 07:54.700
Why am I the only one eating 
the sandwich Hayacchi made?

07:54.700 --> 07:58.330
Oh, shut up. Like it makes 
any difference what <i>you</i> eat.

07:58.830 --> 08:02.200
Wow, harsh! I do have my...

08:04.800 --> 08:06.710
Yum!

08:06.710 --> 08:10.170
Hey, Hayacchi! Let's make this 
a new menu item, too!

08:10.800 --> 08:11.970
Like hell!

08:21.230 --> 08:23.260
Ami's acting weird?

08:23.260 --> 08:25.930
Yes, really weird.

08:25.930 --> 08:29.570
And what's weird about her, specifically?

08:29.930 --> 08:32.490
She's just... normal.

08:32.490 --> 08:33.510
Huh?

08:34.280 --> 08:35.560
Morning.

08:35.560 --> 08:38.740
Like this morning, 
she <i>walked</i> down the stairs...

08:38.740 --> 08:40.480
Thanks for breakfast.

08:40.480 --> 08:42.500
She didn't eat seconds!

08:42.500 --> 08:46.510
And she didn't get a single order wrong 
during her shift yesterday!

08:46.510 --> 08:48.130
Uh, that <i>is</i> normal.

08:48.130 --> 08:49.710
That's just it!

08:49.710 --> 08:53.380
Doesn't it seem weird for Ami-chan 
to act like a normal person?!

08:53.380 --> 08:57.390
She must have hit her head 
really hard somewhere!

08:59.090 --> 09:02.390
We have to get her to the hospital 
before it's too late!

09:02.640 --> 09:04.520
You're being kinda mean.

09:05.510 --> 09:06.650
How am I being mean?!

09:06.650 --> 09:09.270
You're the one who should 
stop fiddling with that laptop!

09:09.270 --> 09:12.150
But I finally managed to buy a new one.

09:12.150 --> 09:14.070
I need to get it all set up.

09:15.110 --> 09:17.120
That one's just gonna break in no time, too.

09:17.120 --> 09:18.070
Stop it.

09:19.080 --> 09:20.830
Thank you for coming by.

09:21.570 --> 09:24.250
You can leave first, Hayacchi.

09:24.640 --> 09:27.710
I'll take care of the cleaning and dishes.

09:27.710 --> 09:30.390
Huh? Uh, sure...

09:32.740 --> 09:35.000
<i>Yeah, she's definitely out of sorts.</i>

09:35.000 --> 09:36.840
<i>Normally, she'd be like...</i>

09:37.800 --> 09:39.880
All done! I'm starving!

09:39.880 --> 09:42.040
Hayacchi, the rest is all yours!

09:42.940 --> 09:47.100
<i>But if I took her to the hospital just 
for that, how would it make me look?</i>

09:47.420 --> 09:48.780
Hey, Akane.

09:48.780 --> 09:51.450
Has anything unusual happened to Ami lately?

09:52.720 --> 09:54.090
Hmm...

09:54.090 --> 09:58.110
Losing her karate practice match, maybe.

09:58.110 --> 10:03.060
She was KO'd in one move by another 
fighter who specializes in kicks.

10:04.340 --> 10:05.820
<i>I get it.</i>

10:05.820 --> 10:09.740
<i>She was a big fish in a small pond, 
and she discovered the ocean.</i>

10:12.070 --> 10:13.800
What did you want to talk about?

10:13.800 --> 10:16.810
Ouka's worried about you.

10:16.810 --> 10:19.210
Says you haven't been yourself.

10:20.160 --> 10:22.970
Not really. I'm the same as I always am.

10:23.560 --> 10:26.180
Is it because you lost your karate match?

10:27.680 --> 10:30.400
What? You did?

10:30.400 --> 10:33.190
Oh. So you knew about that.

10:33.550 --> 10:35.800
Were you up against someone that strong?

10:35.800 --> 10:38.860
Yeah. Someone I've never been able to beat.

10:38.860 --> 10:42.320
No way... Who could be stronger than you?

10:42.920 --> 10:46.760
Someone who was chosen to 
represent Japan at the Olympics.

10:46.760 --> 10:48.780
I-I see...

10:50.160 --> 10:54.340
But it's my own fault I couldn't win.

10:54.340 --> 10:55.680
Huh?

10:55.680 --> 11:00.840
Even my coach told me that some things are 
just impossible, no matter how hard you try.

11:01.680 --> 11:05.690
That there are some walls that 
can't be overcome, so I should give up.

11:07.920 --> 11:11.850
I mean, I know I'm dumb, 
but even I know that much.

11:12.470 --> 11:16.530
I still tried my hardest, 
thinking I might have a chance, but...

11:16.530 --> 11:19.230
That's horrible! 
What coach would tell you that?!

11:19.230 --> 11:21.470
He can't even know that for sure!

11:21.470 --> 11:23.600
You can achieve anything 
if you try hard enough!

11:23.600 --> 11:25.950
Don't give her irresponsible advice.

11:26.250 --> 11:28.250
Talents vary from person to person.

11:28.250 --> 11:30.830
There are some things 
hard work will never get you.

11:31.080 --> 11:33.710
Everyone learns that as they go through life,

11:33.710 --> 11:36.880
and this was Ami's time 
to learn it. That's all.

11:36.880 --> 11:39.090
Well, yeah, but...

11:39.600 --> 11:44.170
That said, I doubt that you lost 
because you lack talent.

11:44.170 --> 11:45.100
Huh?

11:45.100 --> 11:47.640
You're pretty simple-minded.

11:47.640 --> 11:50.480
You probably focused too much 
on a single technique.

11:50.920 --> 11:52.400
Why be stubborn?

11:52.400 --> 11:55.750
Can't you just try to find 
something else you can do?

11:56.400 --> 11:57.940
Something I can do?

11:58.500 --> 11:59.580
That's right.

12:00.450 --> 12:03.450
When you beat up those jerks 
at the Cherry Blossom Festival,

12:03.450 --> 12:04.570
you were genuinely strong.

12:05.150 --> 12:07.830
That's because your goal 
at the time was to win,

12:08.190 --> 12:12.440
and the techniques you used 
were just a means to that end.

12:17.000 --> 12:18.540
Cheer up.

12:18.540 --> 12:21.760
I don't know much about 
all this, but... well...

12:22.010 --> 12:23.760
Just do what you can.

12:25.840 --> 12:27.910
Yeah. You're right.

12:28.600 --> 12:30.760
I don't need to obsess over the Hadoken!

12:30.760 --> 12:33.040
I was able to use a Shoryuken before, too!

12:33.040 --> 12:38.020
So if I really tried, I bet I could pull off 
a Somersault Kick, or even a Cannon Spike!

12:38.020 --> 12:39.030
Cannon...?

12:39.370 --> 12:40.310
Huh?

12:41.920 --> 12:44.200
Ami-chan! Don't tell me you did that in the—

12:44.200 --> 12:47.410
Yep! I really felt like I could do it!

12:48.340 --> 12:49.770
Hadoken!

12:49.770 --> 12:50.790
And when I tried...

12:52.360 --> 12:54.790
I took an axe kick right to the head!

12:55.190 --> 12:58.790
My coach was absolutely furious with me!

12:58.790 --> 13:01.040
He said, "You expected that to work?!"

13:01.040 --> 13:02.810
Of course he'd be furious.

13:02.810 --> 13:05.550
Hey, she's being her usual self now!

13:06.950 --> 13:10.540
I guess it wasn't gonna work, huh? 
I totally knew that.

13:10.540 --> 13:12.570
Thanks, both of you.

13:12.570 --> 13:14.310
I kinda feel like working again!

13:14.310 --> 13:16.890
Do you? Glad to hear it.

13:16.890 --> 13:18.560
Try your hardest, then.

13:18.560 --> 13:21.610
Yeah! I'll make it work, no matter what!

13:21.900 --> 13:23.900
Shoryu—

13:35.030 --> 13:37.560
I didn't do it on purpose! My hand just...

13:38.080 --> 13:40.940
My hand just... slipped...

13:48.260 --> 13:51.760
C-Come on, don't make that scary face!

13:51.760 --> 13:53.720
Wanna give 'em a squeeze?

14:02.150 --> 14:04.150
H-Hayato-kun?

14:04.690 --> 14:07.150
How the hell is that gonna help?!

14:17.040 --> 14:19.930
Huh? Uh... Wait! I'm sorry!

14:19.930 --> 14:22.380
I just thought I should pick it up...

14:22.380 --> 14:24.600
You want me to squeeze yours, too?!

14:24.600 --> 14:26.260
No!

14:26.920 --> 14:30.150
Jeez, they're loud. 
What the heck are they doing?

14:32.400 --> 14:35.700
Let's stop horsing around now.

14:35.640 --> 14:38.020
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

14:35.640 --> 14:38.020
<b>She grew up a little...</b>

14:42.310 --> 14:43.340
Excuse me!

14:43.340 --> 14:44.920
Cinnamon toast, please.

14:44.920 --> 14:45.610
Coming up.

14:46.050 --> 14:48.360
Shiragiku, one cinnamon toast.

14:49.910 --> 14:52.240
Hey, Shiragiku! Are you listening?

14:52.240 --> 14:53.210
Huh?

14:53.690 --> 14:55.240
Oh... I'm sorry!

14:55.240 --> 14:57.130
I spaced out a little.

14:57.130 --> 14:58.500
Listen...

14:58.500 --> 14:59.820
You need to foc—

15:01.910 --> 15:03.310
I tripped.

15:03.310 --> 15:04.680
Hey, are you okay?!

15:04.680 --> 15:06.630
I'm totally fine!

15:06.630 --> 15:10.190
I swear... As if we weren't busy enough.

15:10.190 --> 15:14.260
Riho would normally be here 
to keep them in line...

15:14.890 --> 15:18.940
Hey, Riho! Sorry, but we need your help here!

15:19.520 --> 15:20.960
Riho!

15:20.960 --> 15:23.070
What do you want? No need to yell.

15:23.070 --> 15:26.780
Oh, there you are. 
Sorry, but could you help out at the café?

15:26.780 --> 15:28.920
Three of us isn't enough.

15:28.920 --> 15:31.280
I can't. I have stuff to do today.

15:31.580 --> 15:34.240
Besides, I'm not down for a shift.

15:35.360 --> 15:38.790
Don't think you can just get me 
to help you all the time.

15:38.790 --> 15:42.420
Uh... Well, yeah, that's fair...

15:42.420 --> 15:46.140
I'll get Ouka or Akane, then. 
They're in there, right?

15:46.140 --> 15:46.920
Stop!

15:47.230 --> 15:49.530
You don't want to come in here right now.

15:49.530 --> 15:51.150
Not if you value your life.

15:51.150 --> 15:52.180
Huh?

15:52.180 --> 15:54.200
Quit being dumb and move!

15:54.200 --> 15:55.680
We're insanely busy!

15:55.680 --> 15:57.180
W-Wait!

15:57.550 --> 15:59.270
Hey, someone help at the—

16:13.000 --> 16:14.160
Hello?!

16:14.430 --> 16:16.160
How long are you gonna keep gawking?!

16:19.090 --> 16:20.480
Ow...

16:20.480 --> 16:21.910
I told you so.

16:23.170 --> 16:25.640
How would I have known 
they were taking off their clothes?!

16:25.640 --> 16:28.570
Is that how you guys dress in May?!

16:28.570 --> 16:32.630
We spilled coffee on them, so we wanted 
to wash them before they stained!

16:32.880 --> 16:34.880
Then come to the café when you're done.

16:34.880 --> 16:37.890
Oh, pipe down. We'll go if we feel like it.

16:43.910 --> 16:45.560
Finally done.

16:45.560 --> 16:48.410
Today was a lot busier than most days.

16:49.020 --> 16:53.900
But neither Ouka nor Akane 
ever came down to help,

16:53.900 --> 16:58.160
and Shiragiku and Ami left without 
doing any prep for tomorrow.

16:58.610 --> 17:02.570
The crowd's thinned a bit, 
so I'm not needed anymore, right?

17:03.080 --> 17:05.200
And when Riho finally dragged herself down,

17:05.200 --> 17:07.080
she left as soon as we were done.

17:07.530 --> 17:09.610
I know the café's doing pretty well now,

17:09.610 --> 17:12.840
but they've been slacking off 
too much lately.

17:14.590 --> 17:17.190
Wait, no. That's not right.

17:17.190 --> 17:18.800
Think this over, now.

17:19.730 --> 17:23.320
Ouka and Akane weren't 
even down for a shift today,

17:23.770 --> 17:29.690
and I'm the one who told Riho not to 
work more than she's being paid for.

17:30.110 --> 17:34.690
And prepping for the next day was something 
Shiragiku started to help me out.

17:35.220 --> 17:39.160
And Ami has her club, so insisting 
she come in on weekdays

17:39.700 --> 17:41.300
is kinda selfish of me.

17:43.240 --> 17:45.660
Come on, we're family.

17:45.660 --> 17:48.420
At least help me out when the café's busy.

17:48.420 --> 17:51.880
Okay, fine! Give it a rest, you stupid hag!

17:53.890 --> 17:57.550
They're part-timers... 
and I'm their employer.

17:59.410 --> 18:00.480
It's so pretty!

18:00.480 --> 18:02.560
While we were pretending to be a family,

18:03.070 --> 18:06.700
I forgot about that 
and depended too much on them.

18:12.340 --> 18:15.130
That's right. They're strangers to me.

18:16.740 --> 18:17.950
I don't...

18:18.900 --> 18:20.840
have any family anymore.

18:24.280 --> 18:28.540
<i>We can't keep living 
with our eyes closed to this.</i>

18:29.300 --> 18:32.790
<i>I need to make it clear that 
we're all strangers to each other.</i>

18:33.460 --> 18:35.530
<i>It'll be better for all of us.</i>

18:38.060 --> 18:39.680
Hey, you guys...

18:41.060 --> 18:44.680
Congratulations on two months 
running the café, Master!

18:47.140 --> 18:49.290
You took too long, Hayacchi!

18:49.290 --> 18:51.530
I've been waiting in this pose forever!

18:51.530 --> 18:54.110
Uh, that aside... What is all this?

18:54.400 --> 18:57.860
We're celebrating two months 
since you became the café owner!

18:57.860 --> 19:01.870
T-Two months? 
Not the most impressive number...

19:02.240 --> 19:05.870
Well, at one month, we hated you 
too much to congratulate you.

19:05.870 --> 19:08.880
Huh? Say that again, underwear girl?

19:08.880 --> 19:09.870
Wh-What?!

19:10.280 --> 19:13.230
Riho insisted on a surprise party.

19:13.230 --> 19:16.120
It wasn't easy to decorate 
without you noticing.

19:17.300 --> 19:20.510
Wait, when <i>did</i> you do all this?

19:20.830 --> 19:24.010
When you were trying to get 
into the room earlier today.

19:24.480 --> 19:28.140
You're pretty sharp, 
so I figured you'd notice.

19:28.930 --> 19:32.570
Hey, Riho! Sorry, but we need your help here!

19:32.570 --> 19:34.270
Both of you, start stripping!

19:34.270 --> 19:35.530
What?!

19:35.530 --> 19:37.400
Don't ask questions! Just strip!

19:37.400 --> 19:39.650
So I told them to do that.

19:39.650 --> 19:42.870
Our research has taught us that 
underwear is your weakness.

19:43.410 --> 19:45.470
Thinking back, we took them off in a panic,

19:45.470 --> 19:48.920
but wouldn't it have been less 
embarrassing to just let him find out?

19:48.920 --> 19:52.670
Well, it's all good. 
Not like anyone was hurt.

19:52.940 --> 19:56.780
Also, sorry I didn't help you 
prepare for tomorrow.

19:56.780 --> 19:58.670
I was cooking for this party.

20:00.010 --> 20:01.740
What a spread.

20:01.740 --> 20:03.390
It all looks so fancy!

20:03.050 --> 20:07.680
<b>Master
Congrats on 2 Months</b>

20:03.390 --> 20:05.790
And it all came out of our paychecks,

20:05.790 --> 20:07.210
so you'd better be grateful.

20:08.090 --> 20:10.930
I was making the text plate for the cake

20:10.980 --> 20:13.440
<b>Master 
Congrats on 2</b>

20:11.500 --> 20:14.810
and I panicked a little when I thought 
you were about to see it.

20:15.310 --> 20:19.360
<b>Master 
Congrats on 2 Months</b>

20:15.890 --> 20:19.360
But Ami-chan saved me 
by drawing your attention.

20:19.680 --> 20:20.650
What?

20:21.190 --> 20:23.770
I just tripped and fell, actually.

20:23.770 --> 20:25.820
Oh... You did?

20:25.820 --> 20:28.830
I swear, you guys...

20:28.830 --> 20:33.080
In any case, we're all grateful to you.

20:33.760 --> 20:35.180
One, two...

20:35.180 --> 20:39.030
Thanks for making a place 
where our family can stay together!

20:44.400 --> 20:47.390
So yeah, you're welcome to 
depend on your big sister, okay?

20:47.390 --> 20:49.720
Sorry I was mean to you today.

20:50.010 --> 20:51.690
Also, just so you know,

20:51.690 --> 20:55.480
it was pure coincidence that I was 
in underwear the day we first met!

20:56.020 --> 20:59.480
I know I'm making it harder for Ami 
when I can't work on weekdays

20:59.480 --> 21:02.240
because I have band practice.

21:02.540 --> 21:04.350
I'm totally fine!

21:04.350 --> 21:07.990
I don't mind working weekdays! 
Don't worry about me, Hayacchi!

21:07.990 --> 21:13.720
Don't say sad things like how we're 
"strangers" or a "pretend family."

21:13.720 --> 21:16.420
We <i>are</i> your family, Hayato-kun.

21:17.720 --> 21:19.060
You guys...

21:19.740 --> 21:22.120
You were listening to me 
talking to myself, huh?

21:23.560 --> 21:25.360
Easy now, Hayacchi!

21:25.360 --> 21:27.840
Men never let others see them cry!

21:27.840 --> 21:31.000
I'm not crying! 
And just how much did you hear?!

21:31.000 --> 21:33.280
Oh, all of it!

21:33.280 --> 21:35.180
C'mon, forget about it! Let's eat already!

21:35.660 --> 21:37.390
I'm starving!

21:37.390 --> 21:38.270
Listen—

21:38.270 --> 21:39.190
Hey!

21:39.190 --> 21:41.860
I'm the one who fried the chicken, okay?!

21:43.440 --> 21:45.190
<b></b>Mother

21:44.920 --> 21:46.950
Let's dig in!

21:46.950 --> 21:49.070
I wanna start with the cake!

21:49.070 --> 21:50.950
It's been a long time.

21:51.680 --> 21:54.390
Yes, I know...

21:54.910 --> 21:56.080
Mother.

23:42.060 --> 23:57.080
<b>Episode 7: "A Year in My Life"</b>

23:42.060 --> 23:57.080
<b>Episode 7: "A Year in My Life"</b>

23:42.690 --> 23:45.450
Let me... squeeze your boobs!

23:45.450 --> 23:47.960
Hayacchi's turned into a boob zombie!

23:47.960 --> 23:49.280
What are we supposed to do?!

23:49.280 --> 23:51.880
I'll hold him off! You guys run!

23:53.560 --> 23:56.570
It happens all the time in zombie movies!
